# Command skills

## What does this command do:

A TUI based command line skills chooser to be executed by Claude-code

## Installed from

For Fedora / RHEL (this host, and any other Fedora-based k-fed host) install via the
`kevinpinscoe` DNF repo (source: https://github.com/kevinpinscoe/rpm, served from
`kevinpinscoe.github.io/rpm`), package `skills-tui`:

```
sudo curl -fsSL https://kevinpinscoe.github.io/rpm/kevinpinscoe.repo \
  -o /etc/yum.repos.d/kevinpinscoe.repo
sudo dnf install skills-tui
```

For Mac install via Homebrew: `brew tap kevinpinscoe/homebrew-tap && brew install --cask skills-tui`
For Debian/Ubuntu install via APT — see the skills-tui README for the repo setup.

A pre-built binary is also available from the Releases page for any platform without a
package manager path (Linux x86-64, macOS Apple Silicon, Raspberry Pi 64-bit) — see
https://github.com/kevinpinscoe/skills-tui/releases.

## Command path

The package installs the `skills` command directly on `PATH` (`/usr/bin/skills` via dnf on
Fedora) — no `~/.local/bin` shim needed on this host.

## Command documentation

Docs can be found at https://github.com/kevinpinscoe/skills-tui

## Command options

# Launch the interactive TUI skill chooser
skills

# Show help
skills --help

# Print version and the resolved skills directory
skills --version

# Print categories and skill directories with mtimes, then exit (no chooser)
skills --list

# Order categories/skills: alpha (default), mtime, or recent
skills --sort=recent

# Set a custom skills root directory (default: ~/skills/skills)
SKILLS_DIR=<path> skills
